      "title": "Vercel Connect generates task-scoped Stripe keys for autonomous agents",
      "summary": "Vercel Connect added managed Stripe API keys, allowing teams to generate isolated, task-specific credentials for autonomous agents. The connector automatically provisions restricted keys directly in Stripe accounts, constrained to user-selected permissions rather than sharing broad workspace credentials.",
      "key_facts": [
        "Creates task-specific restricted Stripe API keys for individual agents.",
        "Managed API Key available as a new connection method in Vercel Connect.",
        "Existing MCP and self-managed API key options remain available."
      ],
      "design_implication": "In an authorization settings screen, an administrator configuring an autonomous agent has traditionally faced an all-or-nothing choice between sharing master credentials or blocking automation entirely. Granular key provisioning shifts agent security into a task-scoped delegation flow where each capability requires distinct approval. Start designing agent onboarding flows that surface permission scopes per task rather than granting ambient account-level API access.",
      "implication_lens": "trust_and_risk",
      "visual_need": "illustrate",
      "source_name": "Vercel Blog",
      "source_url": "https://vercel.com/changelog/vercel-connect-adds-managed-stripe-api-keys",
      "source_date": "2026-10-23",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "claim": "Vercel Connect can provision separate restricted Stripe keys per agent task",
          "quote": "can now create a separate for each agent or task. When you create a Stripe connector, you can now choose Managed API Key as the connection method."
        },
        {
          "claim": "Vercel provisions the key in Stripe with user-selected permissions",
          "quote": "Vercel creates the key in your Stripe account, limited to the permissions you pick."
        }
