      "title": "NN/g survey finds UX teams report mixed feelings despite AI speed gains",
      "summary": "A Nielsen Norman Group survey finds that while AI tools accelerate nearly every task for UX practitioners, overall sentiment remains lukewarm. Unreliable model outputs, top-down workplace mandates, and inflated stakeholder expectations diminish perceived productivity gains.",
      "key_facts": [
        "AI speeds up nearly every UX workflow across design and research.",
        "Lukewarm sentiment stems from unreliable output and organizational mandates.",
        "Inflated leadership expectations offset individual time savings."
      ],
      "design_implication": "In a sprint planning session, product designers face compressed timelines driven by leadership assuming generative tools eliminate production overhead. When unvetted AI drafts require extensive manual cleanup, design quality suffers under synthetic velocity. Audit project estimations this week to distinguish rapid drafting from production refinement, ensuring sprint schedules budget explicit time for human critique and verification.",
      "implication_lens": "workflow",
      "visual_need": "none",
      "source_name": "Nielsen Norman Group",
      "source_url": "https://www.nngroup.com/articles/ai-in-ux-survey-26/?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=feed&utm_campaign=rss-syndication",
